 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Totally normal. You don't know anyone there, the waitstaff are only doing their jobs, and everyone else has probably been there for years. That's a nice way to procrastinate about choosing what you really want. If you do bring one, make it something light you' actually finish. Nice. Pick a seat near the window so at least you can see the people across the street. Smart. Lingering is much cheaper than going out again. Order a big pasta shared as an appetiser and you' be ready for anything they throw at you.",
